  "title": "Gerunds and infinitives: Complex forms",
  "description": "Gerund и infinitive имеют сложные формы, которые показывают время и voice более точно.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B2-19-RU",
    "lesson_num": 19,
    "title": "Правила: Gerunds and infinitives: Complex forms",
    "level": "B2",
    "overview": "Gerund и infinitive имеют сложные формы, которые показывают время и voice более точно.",
    "main_rule": "Perfect gerund = having + V3. Perfect infinitive = to have + V3. Passive infinitive = to be + V3. Perfect passive infinitive = to have been + V3.",
    "form": "having + V3. to have + V3. to be + V3. to have been + V3.",
    "when_why": "Используем сложную форму, когда важно показать earlier action или passive meaning.",
    "examples": "He admitted having made a mistake. → Он признал, что совершил ошибку.\nShe seems to have forgotten. → Похоже, она забыла.\nThe report needs to be checked. → Отчёт нужно проверить.\nThe documents appear to have been lost. → Похоже, документы были потеряны.",
    "special_cases": "Выбор формы зависит от time relationship и voice, а не только от main verb.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ He admitted to have made a mistake. → ✅ He admitted having made a mistake.\n❌ He is believed to has left. → ✅ He is believed to have left.\n❌ The report needs checking vs needs to be checked: оба pattern могут встречаться, но здесь source focuses on passive infinitive.",
    "dont_confuse": " earlier action → perfect form. Receiver of action → passive form.",
    "quick_summary": "having + V3 = earlier gerund action.\nto have + V3 = earlier infinitive action.\nto be + V3 = passive.\nto have been + V3 = earlier passive."
  },
